From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 06:10:20 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: a733: Add Timer1

Core power-down idle states need a clock event device outside the cores for
the tick broadcast.

Add Timer1_CPUX. It counts at the rate of the oscillator (26 MHz on the
Cubie A7S), so it takes the oscillator clock.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted on two boards; Timer1 registers with its
interrupt and is the tick broadcast device.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
index 14dbf8f7bd58..c17794b1233a 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
@@ -338,6 +338,15 @@ ccu: clock-controller@2002000 {
 			#reset-cells = <1>;
 		};
 
+		timer@2052000 {
+			compatible = "allwinner,sun60i-a733-timer",
+				     "allwinner,sun8i-a23-timer";
+			reg = <0x02052000 0x50>;
+			interrupts = <GIC_SPI 99 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>,
+				     <GIC_SPI 100 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
+			clocks = <&osc>;
+		};
+
 		uart0: serial@2500000 {
 			compatible = "snps,dw-apb-uart";
 			reg = <0x02500000 0x400>;
